 ### [Sparse Voxel DAG Ray Traversal](1147-sparse-voxel-dag-ray-traversal.md)
-Sparse Voxel DAG (SVDAG) ray traversal is a GPU-based method for efficiently traversing a compressed sparse voxel representation to perform visibility queries (shadows, ambient occlusion) and primary ray intersection. It builds on [Sparse Voxel DAGs](2791-sparse-voxel-dags.md) by exploiting node sharing to reduce memory footprint while maintaining traversal performance comparable to standard Sparse Voxel Octrees (SVOs). Unlike standard SVO traversal, it must handle potential cycles in the graph structure by tracking visited nodes, but avoids complex intersection tests with contours. See [Sparse Voxel DAG Ray Traversal](1147-sparse-voxel-dag-ray-traversal.md).
+Sparse Voxel DAG (SVDAG) ray traversal is a GPU-based method for efficiently traversing a compressed sparse voxel representation to perform visibility queries (shadows, ambient occlusion) and primary ray intersection. It builds on [Sparse Voxel DAGs](2791-sparse-voxel-dags.md) by exploiting node sharing to reduce memory footprint while maintaining traversal performance comparable to standard Sparse Voxel Octrees (SVOs). Unlike standard SVO traversal, it handles shared nodes where multiple parents reference the same child, but avoids complex intersection tests with contours. DAGs are acyclic, so cycle detection is unnecessary; however, shared nodes require careful stack management to avoid redundant processing [G]. See [Sparse Voxel DAG Ray Traversal](1147-sparse-voxel-dag-ray-traversal.md).
 
